Note on section 13 (Remote Network Interaction). Archie is a network service by
design: it runs behind a Slack gateway and users interact with it over a network
without ever receiving a copy. The AGPL is chosen deliberately for that reason —
if you run a modified version of Archie as a service, you must offer its users
access to the corresponding source of your modified version.

